# Greatsword of Tyr's attack trigger taps "up to one" target creature defending player controls: Bot1 chooses none,
# so Bot2's Ornithopter stays untapped. Bot2 answers the trigger by bolting the equipped Ornithopter: as the trigger
# resolves, the creature it would put a +1/+1 counter on is in the graveyard (CR 400.7: a new object), so nothing
# gets the counter, and the Greatsword stays on the battlefield unattached.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Greatsword of Tyr
Ornithopter
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Greatsword of Tyr.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Greatsword of Tyr.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
Bot1.Target()
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Greatsword of Tyr.AttachedTo = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
